From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:53:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/io-pgtable-dart: Honour IO_PGTABLE_QUIRK_NO_PERMS
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

IO_PGTABLE_QUIRK_NO_PERMS asks a format to ignore IOMMU_READ and
IOMMU_WRITE and map everything with full access. The DART format didn't
implement it, so a caller couldn't ask for leaves without the DART
"no read" and "no write" bits.

The A8X (T7000) PCIe DART was brought up with leaves that carry no
protection bits, matching what iOS's AppleS5L8960XDART writes. Support
the generic quirk so the DART driver can select that format per SoC
instead of through a format-private flag. Without the quirk nothing
changes.

Reported-by: Martin Puškáč <martin@icebear.sk>
Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/iommu/io-pgtable-dart.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/io-pgtable-dart.c b/drivers/iommu/io-pgtable-dart.c
index f5a375fa3..9c0b81a57 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/io-pgtable-dart.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/io-pgtable-dart.c
@@ -218,6 +218,9 @@ static dart_iopte dart_prot_to_pte(struct dart_io_pgtable *data,
 {
 	dart_iopte pte = 0;
 
+	if (data->iop.cfg.quirks & IO_PGTABLE_QUIRK_NO_PERMS)
+		prot |= IOMMU_READ | IOMMU_WRITE;
+
 	if (data->iop.fmt == APPLE_DART) {
 		pte |= APPLE_DART1_PTE_PROT_SP_DIS;
 		if (!(prot & IOMMU_WRITE))
